OL,3,GNEWSAHow Windrush children helped shape
OL,4,AWolverhampton
OL,5,
OL,6,F"We pushed barriers, we went into
OL,7,Fspaces where we weren't welcome and we
OL,8,Fdid it unapologetically."
OL,10,FPasvill Lummer, author of The
OL,11,FUnapologetic Generation: Youth,
OL,12,FIdentity and Change in Wolverhampton
OL,13,F1960-1980, migrated from Jamaica as a
OL,14,Fchild in the 1960s.
OL,16,FIn the book, he tells the story of how
OL,17,Fhis peers helped shape Wolverhampton
OL,18,Finto the city it is today.
OL,23,APub: 07-NovQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageBC Eng (W) NewsCReg TVFWeather
FL,360,350,200,160,0,100
